{
  "description": "issue #782: a `tell` two call frames deep persists exactly as one frame deep does. `spec/turtles-and-sprites.md:46` attaches no scoping to `tell`; `ask` is the form the spec explicitly restores (`:58`), and `each` (`:78`) narrows per iteration within the current set — so a procedure body, at any depth, re-scopes nothing. `outer` calls `inner`, which runs `tell :b`; both `procedure-exit` events pass with no restoring addressing `primitive` between them, and afterwards `who` reports :b (turtle 2) while `ycor` reports :b's own y of 20 — not the :a (y 10) the caller had addressed. This pins the current turtle as ONE shared fact rather than a per-call-frame one: with a per-`Environment` cache, each nested call gets its own copy, so the deeper the `tell` the staler the caller's reading.",
